# DURABLE REPRO — a `&` sigil written INSIDE a closure body is silently INERT,
# on BOTH the projection row and the whole-bare-local row.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, `gg check` clean for every row):
#   projection   `bumpi(&b.fd)` in a closure -> prints 10   (want 11)
#   whole local  `bumpi(&loc)`  in a closure -> prints 10   (want 11)
#   ⚠ the IDENTICAL `bumpi(&loc)` at top level prints 11 — so it is the closure
#     body, not the shape, that loses the write.
#
# ⚠ TWO SPELLINGS OF ONE INTENT DISAGREE, which is what makes this a defect
# rather than a limitation: an ASSIGNMENT to a capture (`a.fd = 11`) IS
# classified `BorrowCaptureMode::Mutable`, and the outer read then correctly
# rejects with `error[E_ReadWhileMutCaptured]`. The `&`-through-a-call spelling
# is not classified at all, so `gg check` passes and the write vanishes.
#
# ROOT: `CapturedMutationCollector` (`src/semantic/safety/return_borrows.rs`,
# ~`:243-286`) recognises exactly THREE closure-body mutation forms —
# `Stmt::Assign`, `Stmt::CompoundAssign`, and an `&self` method receiver — and
# has NO arm for `Ownership::MutableBorrow` call args. Its own doc-comment
# states the closed list, which makes this a Core #4 sibling-site hole in an
# enumerated set.
#
# WHY IT IS ON THE WRONG SIDE (the ratified boundary model): a boundary is where
# a value CROSSES FROM ONE SCOPE INTO ANOTHER, and the sigil is written AT the
# crossing. For a closure the crossing is at CAPTURE — and Gorget has no
# capture-list syntax, so it INFERS the mode from the body. An in-body sigil
# therefore sits AFTER the crossing, which is why it can never take effect.
#
# INTENDED (what this fixture asserts): 11 then 11. Under D31 full-strict, `&`
# at a call site IS contractually a write, so the closure must capture mutably
# and the writes must land. (If the language instead decides an in-body sigil is
# unspellable, the reference-grade answer is a CHECK-TIME REJECT — never an
# accepted program whose write silently vanishes.)
#
# ORACLE: ggdef cannot adjudicate — closures are outside the phase-0 subset.
#
# The seeds are COMPUTED, not literals, so const-folding cannot elide the store.

struct B:
    int fd

int seed():
    return 10

void bumpi(int &x):
    x = x + 1

void main():
    B b = B(seed())
    auto f1 = ():
        bumpi(&b.fd)
    f1()
    print(b.fd)

    int loc = seed()
    auto f2 = ():
        bumpi(&loc)
    f2()
    print(loc)
